# `COPY . .` in the build stage takes the whole repo, because `tsc -b` typechecks
# a test that requires `../../../ui.js` and a build scoped to `ui/` cannot resolve
# it. This is what keeps that from also taking the install it just did.
#
# ⚠️ node_modules first and for a reason that is not size: the builder runs
# `npm ci` BEFORE `COPY . .`, so a host `node_modules` copied over the top would
# replace a freshly installed tree with whatever happens to be on the machine
# doing the build — a lockfile-respecting install silently overwritten by one
# that is not.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Built by the image, never copied into it. A stale host bundle landing here would
# be overwritten by the build, but it would also be the thing `--no-build` served
# if the build step were ever skipped.
prototypes/behaviour-ast/ui/dist

.git
.github
docs
*.md
